And a basic component was outlined:

```jsx
// ContentGenerator.js
import { useState } from "react";
import axios from "axios";

function ContentGenerator() {
  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState("");
  const [result, setResult] = useState("");

  const generateContent = async () => {
    const response = await axios.post("http://localhost:8000/generate", { prompt });
    setResult(response.data.content);
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input type="text" value={prompt} onChange={(e) => setPrompt(e.target.value)} />
      <button onClick={generateContent}>Generate</button>
      <p>{result}</p>
    </div>
  );
}

export default ContentGenerator;
```

But there’s **no record of you actually running**:
```bash
npx create-react-app tacf-frontend
```

And we haven’t:
- Deployed the React frontend
- Connected it to the backend
- Set up Tailwind styles or routing

